From: Codex SG2002 port <codex@localhost>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 02:38:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] media: coda: withdraw SG2002 direct NV12 input

The SG2002 Coda980 NV21 path copies the source into a driver-owned
coherent staging buffer before encoding. NV12 bypasses that staging
buffer and programs the source addresses from the user-provided video
buffer directly.

Direct NV12 input corrupts repeated encodes even at 640x480, where no
macroblock-height padding is required. The direct Coda9 source path has
no proven SG2002 source-address or coherency contract, so do not expose
it until that contract is established.

Keep the NV21 interface and its staging conversion, which avoids the
unverified direct-input path.

Signed-off-by: Codex SG2002 port <codex@localhost>
---
 drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-common.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-common.c b/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-common.c
index 6f4f49dd0..ed5a7772c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-common.c
@@ -355,7 +355,6 @@ static const struct coda_video_device sg2002_coda980_encoder = {
 	.type = CODA_INST_ENCODER,
 	.ops = &coda_bit_encode_ops,
 	.src_formats = {
-		V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12,
 		V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV21,
 	},
 	.dst_formats = {
